  "info": {
    "title": "Palletizing line",
    "category": "Manufacturing",
    "description": "Boxes ride an infeed belt past a photo-eye that counts them, then a router whose Python item code sends them to three lines in turn and skips a line with three boxes on its way. Line 1 is a gantry palletizer that picks each box from its moving belt and stacks a pallet pattern of 2 x 2 boxes in two layers; line 2 is a gantry robot picking from a moving belt; line 3 packs by hand, a little slower than the boxes come, so the router skips it now and then. Illustrative figures."
  },
